+\subsection{Procurement}\label{procurement}
+
+\textbf{State.} s = (σ, n, t): σ ∈ \{U, Q, S, K, B\}⁴ records each supplier as untouched, quoted (on time),
+sampled (good yield), qualified or bad; n is actions left; t the elapsed day, capped at
+t̄ = T − min lead + 1. A quote on U goes to B with probability λ, else Q; on S to B with λ/(γ + λ),
+else K. A sample on U goes to B with ρ, else S; on Q to B with ρ/(γ + ρ), else K.
+
+\textbf{Recursion.}
+
+V(σ, 0, t) = D
+
+V(σ, n, t) = max\{ D, max over i with σ\textsubscript{i} = K of A\textsubscript{i}(t), max over (a, i) ∈ R(σ) of Q(σ, n, t; a, i) \}, the last term only when n ≥ 2 and t \textless{} t̄
+
+Q(σ, n, t; a, i) = −c(a, i) + Σ over σ′ of P(σ′ \textbar{} σ, a, i)·V(σ′, n − 1, t + d(a, i))
+
+with R(σ) the quotes on suppliers in U or S and the samples on suppliers in U or Q, and A\textsubscript{i}(t) the best
+award margin with good terms (D if the supplier cannot deliver by T). V counts only spending still to come (information already bought is sunk);
+ties go to the award, then a request, then defer. On all 24 worlds V(U⁴, 10, 0) equals the
+environment's average over the 27 type profiles to within 3·10⁻¹³; its mean is \$450.86.
+
+\textbf{Fixed rules.} Expected loss is the equal-weight mean over the 24 worlds of V* − V\^{}rule.
