+or the reference is wrong.
+
+\textbf{Other checks.} Every committed pack is regenerated byte for byte from its seeds; the Housing
+v14 and v15 receipts replay from their sealed events; trivial agents are reported beside the subjects,
+Procurement's fixed rules are scored exactly, and the briefs were audited for instructions that
+decide the outcome. Uncertainty is computed over worlds, claims name their counterparts, and six
+reported analyses were declared before their runs: Housing v14 and v15 (with v15's two addenda), Procurement's
+declared test, the data-center signalling test and the two agreement confirmatories. Procurement's frozen-control
+diagnostic was also declared before its plays.
+
+\textbf{What it found.} Discovered failures are recorded in an incident log in design,
+operational, tooling and judgment rows that are never deleted: 51 entries about Housing, 57 about Procurement, 90
+about the data center and 23 about Refund on 16 October (Table F.3), with rows added since. Of 25 defects selected for Table F.4, 14 were invisible in any single
+world; the 11 visible ones were found by reading code or sealed bytes, by tracing a case, or in a
+single gate cell (Table F.4). Nine were open when the table was compiled; a later reanalysis from the sealed actions resolves
