 \section*{Abstract}
 
-AI agents can deliver economic value by improving decisions within
-activities such as procurement, contracting and negotiation. The stakes
-of deciding whom to trade with, what to learn and when to commit can
-greatly exceed the cost of performing the task. This motivates evaluating
-agents by the economic outcomes they achieve with information, resources
-and delegated authority. We present AERead, a framework organized around
-economic activities and the parties participating in them. Each case
-specifies a world distribution, seat-specific information, counterpart
-policies and computable references. A shared runtime records execution and
-supports replay of receipt-level scores. References distinguish feasible
-policies, optimal policies under the deciding seat's information and
-full-information bounds, retaining each case's units. Worked examples in
-Housing, Procurement and Data center, with Refund in the cross-case
-analysis, examine information acquisition, bargaining and commitment.
-Quality-control checks reveal how briefs, counterparts and simple-policy
-ceilings change the interpretation of results. Separate verified
-reanalyses reconstruct the Housing and Procurement headline measures from
-sealed records. No case has yet passed every quality-control gate, so the
-contribution is a framework and an evidence-based account of constructing and
-diagnosing evaluations of economic value delivery.
+AI agents are increasingly asked to make economic decisions for a
+principal, such as whom to trade with, what to verify and when to commit. Here a completed
+transaction can destroy value and a refusal can be correct, so
+task-completion or agreement scores cannot tell whether an agent served its
+principal. We present AERead, an environment that scores
+these decisions by the value an agent obtains. Each case defines a
+distribution of economic worlds, seats with private information,
+counterparts with their own interests, and a reference policy whose access
+to information is stated, so that a shortfall separates poor decisions from
+information the agent never had. One runtime executes every case and recomputes
+each score from the sealed record without a model; quality control runs over
+populations of worlds, not single tasks. We build cases in housing, procurement, data-center contracting
+and refunds on this runtime. The counterpart is
+part of the measurement: one agent's earnings lead over another is 42\% of
+the value available in a deal head to head and 7\% against the same scripted
+counterpart. Shortfalls are broken down by stratum and by action
+class; in housing, nearly all of the gap to the reference falls in worlds
+where the tenant's favourite listing is a lemon. Of 25 defects selected from
+our quality-control record, 14 were invisible in any one world. Housing and
+Procurement now pass four of the five quality-control gates and no case passes all five,
+so the results compare named agents on stated worlds rather than rank models. AERead's code is open source: a
+new case supplies its economic rules, worlds and reference, and inherits
+the runtime, replay and the quality-control standard.
